{"analytics_identifier":null,"base_path":"/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-general-comment-on-the-draft-resolution-on-women-in-humanitarian-settings","content_id":"27c72690-fdff-4396-bfe0-0eb4ac0532ac","description":"UK General Comment on the draft resolution on women in humanitarian settings. Delivered by UK Human Rights Ambassador, Eleanor Sanders.","details":{"body":"<div class=\"govspeak\"><p>Thank you, Mr President.</p>\n\n<p>We join others in taking this opportunity to pay tribute to Colombia’s role as penholder in these difficult circumstances and wish to honour once again the memory of Ambassador Gustavo Gallon.</p>\n\n<p>The United Kingdom is pleased to join consensus on this important resolution and thanks the Core Group for its leadership throughout the negotiations. </p>\n\n<p>As humanitarian needs continue to grow in scale and complexity, women and girls remain disproportionately affected by conflict, displacement, disasters and other crises. This resolution places the protection, participation and leadership of women and girls at the centre of humanitarian responses and reinforces the need for a comprehensive, human rights-based approach.</p>\n\n<p>We particularly welcome the references to preventing and responding to gender-based violence. Indeed, conflict-related sexual violence continues to have devastating consequences for survivors, families and communities. Preventing these crimes, supporting survivors, and ensuring perpetrators are held to account must remain a central part of efforts to build sustainable peace and security.</p>\n\n<p>The resolution also highlights the importance of ensuring uninterrupted and non-discriminatory access to healthcare, including sexual and reproductive health services, maternal healthcare, and mental health and psychosocial support. These services are essential to safeguarding the dignity, health and wellbeing of women and girls in crisis situations.</p>\n\n<p>Equally important is its emphasis on the meaningful participation and leadership of women and girls, including women-led organisations, in humanitarian preparedness, response and recovery. Women and girls must be able to shape the decisions that affect their lives and communities.</p>\n\n<p>The United Kingdom is proud to support this resolution.</p>\n\n<p>Thank you.</p>\n</div>","change_history":[{"note":"First published.","public_timestamp":"2026-07-07T15:58:44Z"}],"delivered_on":"2026-07-07T00:00:00+01:00","first_public_at":"2026-07-07T16:58:44.000+01:00","image":{"alt_text":"Eleanor Sanders","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/66f261ca53d61b1b433ee2eb/Eleanor_2.jpg"},"location":"Geneva","political":true,"speech_type_explanation":"Transcript of the speech, exactly as it was delivered"},"document_type":"speech","first_published_at":"2026-07-07T16:58:44+01:00","links":{"available_translations":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-general-comment-on-the-draft-resolution-on-women-in-humanitarian-settings","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-general-comment-on-the-draft-resolution-on-women-in-humanitarian-settings","base_path":"/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-general-comment-on-the-draft-resolution-on-women-in-humanitarian-settings","content_id":"27c72690-fdff-4396-bfe0-0eb4ac0532ac","document_type":"speech","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-07-07T15:58:44Z","schema_name":"speech","title":"UN Human Rights Council 62: UK General Comment on the draft resolution on women in humanitarian settings","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/un-human-rights-council-62-uk-general-comment-on-the-draft-resolution-on-women-in-humanitarian-settings","withdrawn":false}],"government":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","base_path":"/government/2024-starmer-labour-government","content_id":"9dbff654-cdeb-4ebe-9a12-cd4cc20a033e","details":{"current":false,"ended_on":"2026-07-20T00:00:00+00:00","started_on":"2024-07-05T00:00:00+00:00"},"document_type":"government","links":{},"locale":"en","title":"2024 to 2026 Starmer Labour government","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/2024-starmer-labour-government"}],"organisations":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1315","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","base_path":"/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","content_id":"f9fcf3fe-2751-4dca-97ca-becaeceb4b26","details":{"acronym":"FCDO","brand":"foreign-commonwealth-development-office","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de4e90e0710be0354d7/s960_fcdo-main-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de48fa8f5490aff83b4/s300_fcdo-main-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Foreign, Commonwealth<br/>&amp; Development Office"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","withdrawn":false}],"people":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/eleanor-sanders","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/eleanor-sanders","base_path":"/government/people/eleanor-sanders","content_id":"4301c606-5fdc-4e77-bbf1-1dbce629f3c8","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2024-09-24T08:38:41Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Eleanor Sanders","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/eleanor-sanders","withdrawn":false}],"primary_publishing_organisation":[{"analytics_identifier":"D1315","api_path":"/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","base_path":"/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","content_id":"f9fcf3fe-2751-4dca-97ca-becaeceb4b26","details":{"acronym":"FCDO","brand":"foreign-commonwealth-development-office","default_news_image":{"high_resolution_url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de4e90e0710be0354d7/s960_fcdo-main-building.jpg","url":"https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/621e4de48fa8f5490aff83b4/s300_fcdo-main-building.jpg"},"logo":{"crest":"single-identity","formatted_title":"Foreign, Commonwealth<br/>&amp; Development Office"},"organisation_govuk_status":{"status":"live","updated_at":null,"url":null}},"document_type":"organisation","links":{},"locale":"en","schema_name":"organisation","title":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/organisations/foreign-commonwealth-development-office","withdrawn":false}],"roles":[{"content_id":"9066fb8d-4a60-442b-8b3f-6f6c10936714","details":{"body":"<p>The UK’s Ambassador for Human Rights exists to defend and advance human rights and democracy globally. Promoting human rights and the rule of law is fundamental to maintaining stability and preventing conflict and is therefore at the heart of the UK’s interests.  </p>\n\n<p>The Ambassador for Human Rights has 3 main objectives:</p>\n\n<ul>\n  <li>protecting and promoting human rights within the multilateral system, including at the United Nations Human Rights Council</li>\n  <li>working in partnership with countries to support and advance human rights</li>\n  <li>promoting other human rights campaigns in support of the UK’s international priorities</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p>The Ambassador engages with civil society and human rights defenders. Through country missions, she engages with states, human rights institutions and other international partners to champion positive progress made by states, encourage advances and identify areas for collaboration and partnership to support protections and promotion of human rights within those countries.</p>\n","role_payment_type":null},"document_type":"ambassador_role","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2026-03-02T16:11:40Z","schema_name":"role","title":"Ambassador for Human Rights and Deputy Permanent Representative to the United Nations and other International Organisations in Geneva ","withdrawn":false}],"speaker":[{"api_path":"/api/content/government/people/eleanor-sanders","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/government/people/eleanor-sanders","base_path":"/government/people/eleanor-sanders","content_id":"4301c606-5fdc-4e77-bbf1-1dbce629f3c8","document_type":"person","links":{},"locale":"en","public_updated_at":"2024-09-24T08:38:41Z","schema_name":"person","title":"Eleanor Sanders","web_url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/people/eleanor-sanders","withdrawn":false}],"taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/international/human-rights-internationally","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/international/human-rights-internationally","base_path":"/international/human-rights-internationally","content_id":"cb7db7bb-d0b4-4e22-9f0b-58a28c2db38c","details":{"internal_name":"Human rights internationally [P]","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":false},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"parent_taxons":[{"api_path":"/api/content/international","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/international","base_path":"/international","content_id":"37d0fa26-abed-4c74-8835-b3b51ae1c8b2","description":"","details":{"internal_name":"International","notes_for_editors":"","visible_to_departmental_editors":true},"document_type":"taxon","links":{"root_taxon":[{"api_path":"/api/content/","api_url":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/","base_path":"/","content_id":"f3bbde